msgid "Abandoned projects policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/abandoned-projects.rst:4
msgid ""
"This policy describes the process by which a Read the Docs project "
":term:`slug` may be changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/abandoned-projects.rst:6
msgid ""
"If you want to de-list a project's fork from search results, please see "
":doc:`/unofficial-projects`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/abandoned-projects.rst:9
msgid "Rationale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/abandoned-projects.rst:11
msgid ""
"Conflict between the current use of the name and a different suggested "
"use of the same name occasionally arise.  This document aims to provide "
"general guidelines for solving the most typical cases of such conflicts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/abandoned-projects.rst:16
msgid "Specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/abandoned-projects.rst:18
msgid ""
"The main idea behind this policy is that Read the Docs serves the "
"community.  Every user is invited to upload content under the Terms of "
"Use, understanding that it is at the sole risk of the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/abandoned-projects.rst:22
msgid ""
"While Read the Docs is not a backup service, the core team of Read the "
"Docs does their best to keep that content accessible indefinitely in its "
"published form. However, in certain edge cases the greater community's "
"needs might outweigh the individual's expectation of ownership of a "
"project name."
msgstr ""

